<title>USA: Southern Pacific files $1 bln shelf.</title>
<headline>Southern Pacific files $1 bln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southern Pacific Secured Assets Corp, a unit of Imperial Credit Industries Inc, filed Wednesday with the Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $1 billion in pass through certificates and mortgage backed notes.</p>
<p>When combined with previous registration, Southern Pacific will have a total offering of $1,261,463,000 in notes and certificates available for sale.  </p>
<p>The certficates represent an interest in a pool of conventional fixed rate mortgage loans, the filing said.</p>
</text>
